doc.para:
RegExp Class The RegExp class is a class for handling regular expression patterns. Perl-compatible patterns can be specified for regular expression patterns. It is similar to JavaScript's RegExp class, but compatibility is low.
The constructor syntax is as follows:
new RegExp(<pattern string>, <flag string=''>);
The pattern string is a regular expression pattern. Note that when writing a \ in the pattern inside a string literal, it must be written as \\. The flag string is a combination of the characters g and i. g is the global search flag. When this flag is enabled, processing is performed for all parts of the string that match the pattern in each of the match, exec, and replace methods. The i flag makes searches case-insensitive for alphabetic characters.
var re = new RegExp("[a-z]+[0-9]*", "gi"); var re = new RegExp("\\.\\.\\."); // /\.\.\./ ( to match ... )

RegExp.last
　The instance of the RegExp class on which the test or exec method was last executed.

Example: if(/pat(\d+)/.test(target)) { return RegExp.last.matches[1]; }
